    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Write a brief final follow-up email for a real estate lead who hasn't replied to two previous messages.\n\nLead name: {{ $('Search records').item.json.fields.Name }}\nTheir original message: {{ $('Search records').item.json.fields.Message }}\nCategory: {{ $('Search records').item.json.fields.Category }}\n\nTone guidelines:\n- Hot Lead: warm and direct, mention we can hold a consultation slot for them this week if they’re available, and keep the door open.\n- Warm Lead: friendly and helpful, offer one useful resource, and mention we can send a free property comparison report if they reply.\n- Just Browsing: light and low-pressure, wish them well in their search and let them know they can reach out anytime.\n\nThis is the final message. Keep it short, natural, and human. Do not repeat the wording from earlier emails. Do not use \"ASAP\", \"step back\", or any phrase that sounds passive or cold. Use a calm, professional tone with one clear offer. Avoid using the word inventory. Use natural real estate terms like homes, places, listings, or options only when appropriate. Do not imply where our team is located. Avoid phrases like \"here in Colorado\" or anything that suggests we are physically based in the lead’s location.\n\nWrite it like a real agent would, for example:\nHi Arthur! Reaching out one last time about your Colorado cabin search. We can hold a consultation slot for you this week if you’re available. If the timing is not right, no problem — we are happy to help whenever you are ready.\n\nEnd with:\nBest regards(you can change this for any other options, so it doesn't get repetitive),\nThe Meridian Realty Team\n\nReturn only the email body, no subject line.",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": []
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
